title: The column form of a value
tags: [[Data model]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: How a row's value is persisted — its value_type and the columns that type uses — which is also how a log snapshot shows it.

A row's value is persisted in a ''column form'': its `value_type` and the one or two
columns that type uses (`crates/daemon/src/rows.rs`, `encode_value`/`decode_value`).
It is the key-value store's form of a row and the form a log snapshot shows, so it
changes only with a migration.

|!Column |!Holds |
|`value_type` |`nothing` · `string` · `int` · `float` · `bool` · `datetime` · `ref` · `tree_ref` · `refbase` · `externalref` |
|`value_text` |`string` |
|`value_int` |`int`, `bool` (0/1), `datetime` (Unix ms) |
|`value_real` |`float` |
|`value_uuid` |`ref`/`refbase`/`externalref`: the uuid pointed at; `tree_ref`: the parent (the zero uuid for a root) |
|`value_ref_repo` |`externalref`: the repository |
|`value_name` |`tree_ref`: the name as displayed |
|`value_name_bytes` |`tree_ref`: the name's exact bytes (its identity) |

Uuids are stored as their 16 raw bytes. The metarecord's version is stored beside its
rows ([[Metarecord version]]); where the rows sit in the store: [[Store tables]].
